But we're instantiating the helper with (https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/master/src/lib/InstantSearch.js#L103):

``` js
    let helper = algoliasearchHelper(
      this.client,
      this.searchParameters.index || this.indexName,
      this.searchParameters
    );
```

So why would it solve the undefined index? With that code the underlying index name can never be `undefined`, isn't it?
